# Test build 2's switches. Read at every start of play-pkg-0381tb2.sh; no rebuild. All off.
# To turn one on, remove its "# ". The first line of the start's log names what was on.
# Turn on one at a time, or a result cannot be tied to a switch. Ordered by expected cost, lowest first.
# A line must be exactly NAME=value as below. Anything else is ignored and the log gives its line number. The last valid line for a name wins.
# GPU_CHECK_YZ also takes <y> or <y>:<z>, each from 1 to 99999. A commented line means off, whatever the environment held.
# This file beats bc5-run.env and bc5-pkg.env: a switch set in either is off unless it is on here.
# Only ARGS_WB=first has a measured cost (within noise). The others have none on record.
#
# No extra packets:
# BC5_DIRECT_GPU_CHECK_YZ=1
# BC5_DIRECT_FORCE_START_000=1
#
# Extra packets only about 145 times a second:
# BC5_DIRECT_ARGS_WB=first
# BC5_DIRECT_ARGS_FLUSH=first
#
# Extra packets on every checked draw or dispatch, never run on the GPU:
# BC5_DIRECT_ARGS_FLUSH_DRAWS=1
# BC5_DIRECT_GPU_CHECK_ZERO=1
#
# Expensive: about 24,000 times a second. "all" never ran alone.
# BC5_DIRECT_ARGS_FLUSH=all
# BC5_DIRECT_ARGS_WB=all
#
# Catchers, off until a question needs them. Journals write through the page cache and can fill the disk: one long journal took 38 GB in on-3, so keep the session short.
# BC5_DIRECT_DRAW_ARGS_JOURNAL=1
# BC5_DIRECT_DISPATCH_JOURNAL=1
#
# A catcher that forces a fault's position: the title's graphics buffer of exactly this many dwords. Without the restore it faulted 3 of 3 times (F685).
# BC5_DIRECT_CHAIN_BREAK_AT=12673
#
# Can hang the GPU and reboot the box: the low-address slot has never run.
# BC5_DIRECT_ARGS_COPY=1
